  "id": "COMPOUND:7839 - PROTEIN:802",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Icosapent ethyl and the Proteasome subunit beta type-5, as it is indirectly linked through multiple pathways involving 5-hydroxytryptamine receptors. Icosapent ethyl is known to target several 5-hydroxytryptamine receptors, including 5-HT5A and 5-HT2B, which in turn are targets of other compounds such as tropicamide and PF-03187207. These compounds further target the Proteasome subunit beta type-5, indicating a possible downstream effect of Icosapent ethyl on this enzyme. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent but moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with varying degrees of support from different targets. The mechanism appears to involve the modulation of 5-HT receptors, which may influence the activity of the Proteasome subunit beta type-5, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence is supported by multiple independent pathways, but further research is needed to confirm the direct or indirect role of Icosapent ethyl in regulating this enzyme.",
